# Klingon (tlhIngan Hol) translation for SeedSigner.
# Latin transliteration; the pIqaD script needs a font the device does not carry.
#
# Intentionally partial. Roots are attested in Marc Okrand's Klingon Dictionary;
# multi-word entries use canonical word-building (yI- imperative, -moH causative,
# -Ha' undo, -lIj your, -mey plural). Untranslated strings fall back to English,
# which includes every security warning: Klingon has no vocabulary for "Native
# Segwit" or "derivation path", and inventing some on a bitcoin signing device
# would be worse than leaving it in English.
#
# Notable choices:
#   Settings -> SeHlaw   "control panel" (attested)
#   Seeds    -> tIrmey   tIr is "grain"; English "seed" is the same metaphor
#   Verify   -> yI'ol    'ol is "verify" (attested)
#
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: seedsigner 0.8.7\n"
